0result.sql is the most robust and readable of the three options.  
• It first isolates only active stations in a CTE, guaranteeing that every subsequent join involves active stations.  
• It uses SAFE_CAST when comparing the string end_station_id to numeric station_id, avoiding runtime errors from non‑numeric values.  
• It explicitly enforces the “start ≠ end station” rule and the “same district” rule before performing the final aggregation.  
These precautions make 0result.sql both safe and faithful to the stated requirements, so it is the best choice.